{
  "id": "COMPOUND:4298 - PROTEIN:6339",
  "verbalization": "Estriol is implicated in the regulation of Liver X receptor (LXR) alpha and beta through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Estriol acts as a target of several enzymes, which in turn interact with LXR. Specifically, Estriol is linked to Ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2, which is targeted by Hydroxysaikosaponin C, and this compound further targets LXR. Similarly, Estriol is also linked to 11-cis retinol dehydrogenase, which is targeted by 2-[(4S)-4-hydroxy-3,6-dioxodioxan-4-yl]acetic acid, and this compound also targets LXR. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Estriol influences LXR activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a network of indirect relationships, suggesting that Estriol may modulate LXR through a series of enzymatic and receptor-mediated interactions, though the precise molecular mechanisms are not fully understood.",
